  "problem": "C63 optional scoped helpers used the required blocking path, so already-owned queued keys could occupy helpers without initializing new work. Descriptor counts did not identify actual ownership.",
  "implementation": "Cell::try_get_or_init returns ready values, claims an empty cell or skips an already-owned cell without registering a waiter. Both APIs share the exact owner, OnceLock publication, panic recovery and TLS ancestor guard. Only the optional queued scoped key skips Busy; a newly owned anchor uses all original required dependency waits. Existing required consumers still resolve every offered writer. Actual ready/busy/owned outcomes are counted at the queued key, without attributing recursive work to that origin. Per-root scoped joining, bounded helper permits, queue capacity and 32-writer batches remain intact.",
