  "claims": "Counters cover profile lifetime including one warmup and one measured region. Scoped attempted keys classify at the actual call: ready includes cached failure, owned includes a newly initialized failure, busy skips another initializer; attempts also include any pre-claim lookup failure. Drained counts successful ready/owned results. These successful runs have attempts=ready+busy+owned and drained=ready+owned. Only 3.24\u20134.76 percent of scoped attempts owned a new key; ready was 63.13\u201370.78 percent and busy 24.94\u201333.60 percent. These events do not measure time shares or useful CPU utilization. Waiter-picked helpers still use the blocking path and are not classified.",
  "observer_definition": "Target/helper counts and longest tasks remain separate; physical-thread unions include both. Helper success means no error and includes skipped Busy calls. Target percentiles exclude helper attempts; the tail ends at the last target/helper finish. In-flight spans include blocking/preemption. Process CPU includes service/shader and observer work. Separate observer runs under changed host load are not causal speedup comparisons.",
